    <li>Bucephalandra "Pygmea" prefers stable water conditions.</li>
    <li>Ideal temperature range: 71-82.5°F (21.5-28°C) or 72-82°F (22-28°C).</li>
    <li>pH range: 5.5-7.5 or 6.0-7.5.</li>
    <li>Maintain clean, well-filtered water with proper flow. Bucephalandra species do better in stable tanks with matured biological systems.</li>
    <li>Some hardness (GH) is beneficial; preferably 5 GH and above.</li>
</ul>

<h2>CO2 and Fertilization</h2>
<ul>
    <li>CO2 injection is not mandatory for survival but can significantly enhance growth and coloration.</li>
    <li>Bucephalandra primarily absorbs nutrients from the water column, so a liquid fertilizer can be beneficial.</li>
    <li>Regular dosing of a comprehensive liquid fertilizer will support healthy development.</li>
    <li>Adequate fertilization is important, especially with a balanced NPK + Fe (nitrogen, phosphorus, potassium + iron) fertilizer.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Planting and Substrate</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Bucephalandra "Pygmea" is an epiphytic plant and should not have its rhizome buried in the substrate, as this can lead to rot.</li>
